From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: let a cross file answer the strftime year check

meson.build finds the strftime modifier that prints a four-digit year by
compiling a probe and running it. The FTS5 check just above it already
knows a cross build cannot do that and reads sqlite3_has_fts5 from the
cross file's [properties] instead; the strftime probe has no such escape
and configure stops:

  meson.build:188:23: ERROR: Can not run test applications in this cross
  environment.

Give it the same escape: when cross compiling without an exe_wrapper,
take strftime_year_modifier from the cross file, and fail with a message
naming the property (and the answer for glibc and musl, %4Y) if it is
missing. A native build is untouched.

Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -185,6 +185,14 @@
 ##################################################################
 # Get an appropriate 4-digit year modifier for strftime
 ##################################################################
+# Like sqlite3_has_fts5 above: a cross build cannot run the probe, so it
+# takes the answer from the [properties] section of the cross file instead.
+if meson.is_cross_build() and not meson.has_exe_wrapper()
+  year_modifier = meson.get_cross_property('strftime_year_modifier', '')
+  if year_modifier == ''
+    error('Please assign an appropriate value for strftime_year_modifier in the [properties] section of your crossfile (glibc and musl: %4Y)')
+  endif
+else
 result = cc.run('''
   #define _TIME_BITS 64
   #define _GNU_SOURCE
@@ -216,6 +224,7 @@
 else
   year_modifier = result.stdout()
 endif
+endif
 
 ##################################################################
 # Check for libtracker-data and libtracker-fts: Unicode support
